# Combat-PoD Manual Move Authoring Guide

This guide covers adding a new combat move.

For the system internals (variable namespace, execution phases,
result codes, tier model, capability flags, design decisions), see
`COMBAT_REFERENCE.info`. This guide focuses on the
authoring workflow; the reference doc is the source of truth for
what each piece does at runtime.

---

## The four artifacts every move needs

Every combat move is glued together from four pieces:

| # | Artifact | What it is | Where it lives |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **A `POD_init_combat_move` call** | Builds the runtime story_cycle that holds the move's mechanics | `devpod/common/scripted_effects/POD_combat/pod_combat_move_list_effects.txt` |
| 2 | **A hidden decision** | Holds the unlock requirements (trait / faith / perk gates) | `devpod/common/decisions/POD_combat/pod_combat_move_decisions.txt` |
| 3 | **Three localization keys** | Display name + dynamic-stat desc + flavor tooltip | `devpod/localization/english/gui/pod_combat_l_english.yml` |
| 4 | **A texture reference** | Optional but recommended — visual icon for the loadout-editor card | One of the `@texture_*` constants at the top of `pod_combat_move_decisions.txt` |

If any of #1, #2, or #3 is missing, the move either fails to load,
fails to gate correctly, or shows broken text in the UI. #4 is
cosmetic but hidden decisions without a `picture` show as a generic
placeholder.

---

## Quick start: a minimal damage move

This is the absolute smallest example — a vanilla physical attack
called "Power Punch" that any character can use, deals 3 damage,
costs 4 AP, and falls into the ATK category.

### Step 1: hidden decision

Append to `devpod/common/decisions/POD_combat/pod_combat_move_decisions.txt`:

```
POD_combat_move_power_punch = {
    picture = { reference = @texture_atk }
    is_valid_showing_failures_only = {
        always = yes
    }
    decision_group_type = hidden
    ai_check_interval = 0
    confirm_text = blank_line
}
```

`@texture_atk` is one of the four illustration constants declared at the top of `pod_combat_move_decisions.txt` (one per combat category — see "Pictures (texture constants)" below).

### Step 2: localization

Append to `devpod/localization/english/gui/pod_combat_l_english.yml`:

```yaml
l_english:
 POD_combat_move_power_punch: "Power Punch"
 POD_combat_move_power_punch_desc: "[PODCombatMoveDesc('POD_combat_move_power_punch')]"
 POD_combat_move_power_punch_tooltip: ""
```

The three keys are mandatory: name, `_desc` (which calls the macro that
renders the rich tooltip card from the move's runtime variables), and
`_tooltip` (an short description of the skill). 

### Step 3: registration call

Every move story_cycle is created by a `POD_init_combat_move` block inside the body of `POD_initialize_combat_moves`, which fires once at `on_game_start`.


Open `devpod/common/scripted_effects/POD_combat/pod_combat_move_list_effects.txt` and add this block inside the `POD_initialize_combat_moves = { ... }` body:

```
POD_init_combat_move = {
    DECISION   = POD_combat_move_power_punch
    SKILL_KEY  = power_punch
    CATEGORY   = ATK
    CONFIG     = base_physical
    AP_COST    = @ap_cost_major     # 4
    AI_WEIGHT  = 12
    TARGETING  = single_enemy
}
scope:new_combat_move = {
    POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage = { VALUE = @damage_medium }   # 3
}
```

The `@ap_cost_*` / `@damage_*` / `@energy_cost_*` / etc. parse-time constants live at the top of `pod_combat_move_list_effects.txt` — see "Setter reference" below for how to use them and "Numeric constants reference" at the end of this guide for the full table. Raw integers work too.

On the next game-start the move is created, added to the global `POD_combat_moves` list, and visible in the loadout editor — gated by the `always = yes` in the decision (anyone can equip it).

---

## The constructor: `POD_init_combat_move`

Every move starts with one call to this. All seven parameters are
**required**:

| Parameter | Values | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `DECISION` | `POD_combat_move_<key>` | The hidden decision holding this move's unlock gate. Must match the decision you author. |
| `SKILL_KEY` | lowercase identifier | Internal flag identifier. Matches the suffix of the decision name. Don't include `POD_combat_move_` prefix. |
| `CATEGORY` | `ATK` / `DEF` / `CTL` / `PWR` | Loadout category. Caps at 4 equipped per category. Drives icon coloring and grouping. |
| `CONFIG` | lowercase identifier | Section grouping in the loadout editor (e.g., `base_physical`, `celerity`, `bloodsorcery_advanced`). Free-form; pick something matching the move's flavor. |
| `AP_COST` | integer 1-6 (typically) | Action-point cost of the move. Affordability is checked at click time. |
| `AI_WEIGHT` | integer | Base AI selection weight. See "Choosing AI weights" below. |
| `TARGETING` | one of the targeting flags | How the move picks its target. See targeting reference below. |

After the constructor call, the body of `scope:new_combat_move = { ... }`
is where all the optional setters go.

### Targeting flags

| Flag | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `single_enemy` | Hits the actor's currently selected enemy target. Most attack moves. |
| `single_ally` | Hits a single ally on the actor's team. Most heal/buff moves that benefit a teammate. |
| `single_pc` | Always targets slot 0 (the player character). Used by NPC moves that specifically protect or attack the PC. |
| `self` | Targets the actor themselves. Self-buffs, defensive stances. |
| `team_enemy` | AoE — hits every enemy in slots 5-9. |
| `team_ally` | AoE — hits every ally in slots 1-4 (and slot 0 if applicable). |

The AI's swap layer dispatches on `targeting` alone: `single_ally` picks
the first alive same-team ally; `single_pc` picks slot 0; `single_enemy`
keeps the actor's turn-start target. Target-priority hints
(wounded / healthy / round_robin / threat) are parked outside `devpod/`

---

## Setter reference

All setters go inside `scope:new_combat_move = { ... }` after the
constructor call. Order doesn't matter, but grouping by category
(costs, damage, buffs, flags) keeps the entry readable.

You can use raw integers anywhere a value is expected, OR you can
reference one of the `@-constants` defined at the top of
`pod_combat_move_list_effects.txt` (e.g. `@damage_minor` = 2,
`@ap_cost_medium` = 3). The constants are just convenience macros for
parse-time substitution; both forms work identically.

### Costs

| Setter | Parameter | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| `POD_combat_move_set_energy_cost = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Drains the actor's splat-specific energy pool — Blood for vampires, Gnosis for shifters, Pathos for wraiths, Glamour for changelings, static stress for hunters/mortals, etc. The `required_trait` gate on the hidden decision should ensure the actor has the right pool. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_stress_cost = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Adds Mental Strain to the PC. PC-only — AI doesn't pay this. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_gold_cost = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Subtracts gold. PC-only. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_prestige_cost = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Subtracts prestige. PC-only. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_piety_cost = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Subtracts piety. PC-only. |

### Damage and damage routing

| Setter | Parameter | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| Capability flags (see "Pipeline shape via capability tags" below) | one or more `POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = X }` calls | Compose the four capability tags (`checks_spirit_gate`, `requires_hit_roll`, `checks_guard`, `checks_stance`) to express the pipeline. The runtime reads these directly; no separate attack-type variable exists at runtime. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_damage_source = { VALUE = X }` | `fire` / `cold` / `lightning` / `sun` / `silver` / `gold` / `holy` / `balefire` | Damage flavor flag, routes to the matching PoD death_reason. Forces aggravated wounds against vulnerable splats — silver vs werewolves, sun vs vampires, holy vs the unholy, etc. **Omit for generic damage** with no special routing. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage = { VALUE = N }` | integer | HP damage dealt to the target. Defaults to superficial. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_damage_type_aggravated = yes` | (no params) | Forces the move's HP damage to land as aggravated regardless of source. Use for moves that should be unsoakable / hard to heal. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_morale_damage = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Morale damage. Routes through its own auto-hit pipeline; ignores capability flags / `damage_source`. Spills over as Mental Strain on the target character (`pod_combat_morale_stress_multiplier` = 5x). |
| `POD_combat_move_set_self_damage = { VALUE = N }` | integer | HP damage dealt to the **actor** (themselves) when the move fires. Always superficial, soakable, ignores stances. Used for reckless attacks. |

#### Pipeline shape via capability tags

The four capability tags compose the pipeline shape:

| Pipeline | Tags to set | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| **Physical** (default — full pipeline) | `checks_spirit_gate`, `requires_hit_roll`, `checks_guard`, `checks_stance` | Spirit gate + stealth/dodge + hit roll + guard + soak. Can be soaked, dodged, guarded, missed against incorporeal targets. |
| **Supernatural** (auto-hit, skips guard) | `checks_stance` only | Stealth + dodge only. Auto-hits past evasion, ignores guard, soak still applies. Hits incorporeal targets. |
| **Mental** (morale-only) | `checks_stance` only + omit `hp_damage`, set `morale_damage` instead | Same flag profile as supernatural; differentiated by routing morale damage through its own pipeline. |

`POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = checks_spirit_gate }` etc. is the canonical way to set each. To author a guard-bypassing physical strike, set `checks_spirit_gate`, `requires_hit_roll`, `checks_stance` (drop `checks_guard`). To author an always-hits physical strike, drop `requires_hit_roll`.

### Healing

| Setter | Parameters | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| `POD_combat_move_set_hp_heal = { VALUE = N TYPE = X }` | integer + `superficial` / `aggravated` | Heals the target. `superficial` only refills below the aggravated ceiling; `aggravated` reduces aggravated wound boxes first then spills into superficial. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_morale_heal = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Restores morale. Caps at the morale max (20). |

### Rider conditions (gate heal / morale damage / self-damage on outcome)

By default a heal, morale-damage, or self-damage payload fires
unconditionally when its setter is present. To make any of those
payloads fire only on a specific outcome of the move's primary
HP-damage step, set the matching condition flag:

| Setter | Parameter | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| `POD_combat_move_set_heal_condition = { VALUE = X }` | `always` / `on_hp_damage` / `on_contact` / `on_miss` | Gates `hp_heal` on the §6 outcome. Default = always. Drain attacks (vampire bite, soul-rend) use `on_hp_damage`. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_morale_damage_condition = { VALUE = X }` | same flags | Gates `morale_damage` on the §6 outcome. Default = always. Use `on_hp_damage` for "morale damage rides on a landed wound", `on_miss` for "intimidation only fires on the whiff", etc. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_self_damage_condition = { VALUE = X }` | same flags | Gates `self_damage` on the §6 outcome. Default = always (matches the existing reckless-charge pattern). Use `on_miss` for "you only hurt yourself when you whiff." |

| Flag value | Fires when the §6 outcome is |
|---|---|
| `always` | any (default if condition unset) |
| `on_hp_damage` | HP damage landed (outcome=attack + attack_result=hp_damage) |
| `on_contact` | any physical contact (outcome=attack + attack_result ∈ hp_damage / guard_blocked / soaked) |
| `on_miss` | miss / dodge / stealth (outcome=attack + attack_result ∈ missed / dodged / stealthed) |

### Tier buffs and debuffs

Three magnitudes (small/medium/large = ±10/±20/±30) × two durations
(round / combat) × two stats (soak / hit) × two directions (buff /
debuff) = 8 setters. Each takes a `TIER` of `1`, `2`, or `3`.

```
POD_combat_move_set_soak_buff_round   = { TIER = 2 }   # +20 soak this round only
POD_combat_move_set_soak_buff_combat  = { TIER = 3 }   # +30 soak for the whole combat
POD_combat_move_set_soak_debuff_round = { TIER = 1 }   # -10 soak on target this round
POD_combat_move_set_soak_debuff_combat = { TIER = 2 }
POD_combat_move_set_hit_buff_round    = { TIER = 1 }   # +10 hit chance this round
POD_combat_move_set_hit_buff_combat   = { TIER = 2 }
POD_combat_move_set_hit_debuff_round  = { TIER = 1 }   # -10 hit chance on target this round
POD_combat_move_set_hit_debuff_combat = { TIER = 2 }
```

A higher tier overwrites a lower; reapplying the same tier or below
is blocked by the redundancy gate (the loadout SGUI greys the button,
the AI selector excludes the candidate). Buffs apply to the actor,
debuffs to the target.

### Parametric non-tier modifiers

| Setter | Parameter | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| `POD_combat_move_set_ap_gain = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Grants the actor +N AP this turn. Stacks across uses. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_ap_drain = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Drains N AP from the target's next turn (min 1 AP after drain). |
| `POD_combat_move_set_initiative_debuff = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Subtracts N from the target's next-round initiative roll. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_retaliate_damage = { VALUE = N }` | integer | Sets the damage value the actor deals back when their `retaliate_if_hit` or `retaliate_if_missed` flag fires. **Pair this with `POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = retaliate_if_hit }` (or `_if_missed`)** — without the flag, the retaliate_damage is set but nothing reads it. |
| `POD_combat_move_set_retaliate_agg = yes` | (no params) | Marks retaliation damage as aggravated. |

### Presence flags

A presence flag is just "this attribute is set." Use the generic
setter:

```
POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = bypass_dodge }
```

Available flag names:

| Flag | Effect |
|---|---|
| `set_guard` | Activates Guard stance on the actor (next physical attack against them is blocked). |
| `dodge` | Activates Dodge stance (next attack of any type auto-misses). |
| `stealth` | Activates Stealth (next incoming attack auto-misses + actor's next attack gets +30 hit). |
| `bypass_dodge` | This attack ignores the target's Dodge stance — strips the stance from the target's workspace before the contact resolver reads it. |
| `bypass_stealth` | This attack breaks the target's Stealth (and reverses the +30 hit bonus). |
| `remove_guard` | Strips the target's Guard stance without dealing damage. AI gets +15 weight when target is guarding. |
| `retaliate_if_hit` | Sets a counter-attack stance — if the actor is hit (or contacted via guard/soak), they deal `retaliate_damage` back to the attacker. |
| `retaliate_if_missed` | Same, but fires when the attacker misses, dodges, or whiffs against stealth. |
| `drain` | Marks an `hp_heal` as life-stealing — authors should pair this with `POD_combat_move_set_heal_condition = { VALUE = on_hp_damage }` so the heal actually gates on a landed hit. (Setting just the `drain` flag without the heal_condition setter only sets the flag — the runtime gates on heal_condition, not on `drain` directly.) |
| `is_starter_move` | Marks the move as part of the PC's default loadout. The configure decision seeds these. Also signals to the AI selector "this is a generic baseline move" — the +10 trait-gate bonus does NOT apply. Reserve for the few baseline starters every character should have. |
| `summons_<creature>` | Mid-combat summon (e.g. `summons_wraith`); the generator emits `POD_combat_move_set_summon = { RECIPE = <creature> }`. §14b of `POD_execute_combat_move` fires the generic `pod_combat_summon_combatant_glue_effect` (in `pod_combat_summon_effects.txt`), which creates a fresh combatant, applies the recipe via `pod_combat_apply_summon_recipe_effect`, and seats it on the caster's team mid-fight (`pod_combat_add_ally_midfight_effect` / `_add_enemy_midfight_effect`). It sits out the cast round, joins initiative next round, posts a named "joins the fray" log row, and is despawned at combat end. Author with `TARGETING = self` and no `hp_damage`. A NEW creature type = one `else_if` branch in `pod_combat_apply_summon_recipe_effect`, nothing else. |

**Note on guard bypass.** There's no `bypass_guard` flag — a
guard-bypassing physical strike is authored by *omitting*
`checks_guard` from the capability tags. See "Pipeline shape via
capability tags" above.

**Aggravated retaliation.** Pair `POD_combat_move_set_retaliate_agg = yes`
with `POD_combat_move_set_retaliate_damage = { VALUE = N }` and
the matching `retaliate_if_hit` / `retaliate_if_missed` flag.
The `retaliate_agg` setter only marks the counter-attack as
aggravated; the actor's own primary damage is independent
(controlled by `POD_combat_move_set_damage_type_aggravated`).

