## Localization keys

Three keys per move, in any `.yml` file under
`devpod/localization/english/`. The file must start with a UTF-8 BOM
and the `l_english:` header.

```yaml
l_english:
 POD_combat_move_<skill_key>: "Display Name"
 POD_combat_move_<skill_key>_desc: "[PODCombatMoveDesc('POD_combat_move_<skill_key>')]"
 POD_combat_move_<skill_key>_tooltip: "A short narrative description of the skill"
```

| Key | What it does |
|---|---|
| Bare `POD_combat_move_<skill_key>` | Short display name. Shown in the loadout editor and the move bar. AP cost is appended automatically by `POD_combat_move_title`, so don't include it. |
| `_desc` | Decision description. CK3 auto-resolves `<decision_id>_desc` when rendering the loadout editor's full card; the macro inside renders the move's costs, damage, flags, etc. live from the runtime story_cycle variables. **Always use the macro form shown above** — writing custom prose here would override the dynamic stat block. |
| `_tooltip` | A short narrative description of the skill. |

---

## Worked example: a discipline attack

Let's walk through `Breath of the Basilisk`, a real Serpentis-advanced
move that's an aggravated AoE supernatural attack. Looking at it gives
a complete reference for a complex move.

### Constructor

```
POD_init_combat_move = {
    DECISION   = POD_combat_move_breath_of_basilisk
    SKILL_KEY  = breath_of_basilisk
    CATEGORY   = PWR
    CONFIG     = serpentis
    AP_COST    = @ap_cost_maximum  # 6
    AI_WEIGHT  = 12
    TARGETING  = team_enemy
}
```

### Setters

```
scope:new_combat_move = {
    POD_combat_move_set_energy_cost = { VALUE = @energy_cost_minor }  # 2 Blood
    # Supernatural pipeline: only checks_stance (auto-hit, skips
    # guard, ignores spirit gate). Drops the three flags physical
    # would have set.
    POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = checks_stance }
    POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage = { VALUE = @damage_minor }           # 2 damage per enemy
    POD_combat_move_set_damage_type_aggravated = yes
    POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = bypass_dodge }
}
```

### Hidden decision

```
POD_combat_move_breath_of_basilisk = {
    picture = { reference = @texture_serpentis }
    is_valid_showing_failures_only = {
        has_trait = serpentisadvanced
        has_perk = breath_of_the_basilisk_perk
    }
    decision_group_type = hidden
    ai_check_interval = 0
    confirm_text = blank_line
}
```

### Localization

```yaml
 POD_combat_move_breath_of_basilisk: "Breath of the Basilisk"
 POD_combat_move_breath_of_basilisk_desc: "[PODCombatMoveDesc('POD_combat_move_breath_of_basilisk')]"
 POD_combat_move_breath_of_basilisk_tooltip: "Exhale a paralyzing miasma over every enemy"
```

### How it plays

A Setite vampire with Serpentis at advanced level, who has unlocked
the breath_of_the_basilisk perk, sees this in their PWR loadout slot.
Costs 6 AP (a full turn) + 2 Blood. Deals 2 aggravated damage to
*every* enemy in slots 5-9, supernatural pipeline so it auto-hits
through their hit chance, and ignores their Dodge stance. Excellent
crowd-clear at the cost of being prohibitively expensive on a
single-enemy fight.

