## Worked example: a vampiric drain attack

A made-up "Soulrend" move — physical attack that heals you on hit,
gated behind Vicissitude (a hypothetical setup):

```
POD_init_combat_move = {
    DECISION   = POD_combat_move_soulrend
    SKILL_KEY  = soulrend
    CATEGORY   = ATK
    CONFIG     = vicissitude_advanced
    AP_COST    = @ap_cost_major          # 4
    AI_WEIGHT  = 12
    TARGETING  = single_enemy
}
scope:new_combat_move = {
    POD_combat_move_set_energy_cost    = { VALUE = @energy_cost_tiny }   # 1
    POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage      = { VALUE = @damage_medium }      # 3
    POD_combat_move_set_hp_heal        = { VALUE = @healing_minor TYPE = superficial }  # 2
    POD_combat_move_set_heal_condition = { VALUE = on_hp_damage }
    POD_combat_move_set_flag           = { NAME = drain }
}
```

`heal_condition = on_hp_damage` is what actually gates the heal on the attack landing — if the swing misses, dodges, or is stealth-evaded, the runtime's §9 rider check fails and no heal happens. The `drain` flag itself is cosmetic at runtime: the loadout editor's tooltip swaps "Heal 2" → "Drain 2" when the flag is set so players see at a glance that this is a vampiric heal, but the gating is in `heal_condition`. 

