## Choosing values: guidelines from existing moves

### AP cost

| Cost | Use for | Examples in current roster |
|---|---|---|
| 1-2 | Light moves you might use multiple per turn | Quick Jab (3), most ap_gain utilities |
| 3 | Standard moves — bread and butter | Strike (4 actually), Feint, Intimidate, most discipline taps |
| 4 | Bigger swings — typically 1-2 per turn | Heavy attacks, mid-tier disciplines |
| 5 | Heavy moves | Some combat-duration buffs, intimidating shouts |
| 6 | Signature ultimates — one per turn | Reckless Charge, Heavy Blow, AoE disciplines like Breath of the Basilisk |

The action economy is 6 AP per turn, so AP 6 means the entire turn.
AP 3 is half-turn and lets you mix two medium moves. AP 1-2 lets
chains of cheap actions. Don't make every move AP 6 — you flatten the
tactical decision space.

### Energy cost

| Cost | Use for |
|---|---|
| 2 | Most discipline moves at base level |
| 4 | Advanced disciplines or signature uses |

### HP damage

| Damage | Use for | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Light/cheap moves | Quick Jab template |
| 2 | Standard | Strike (the basic starter), most disciplines |
| 3 | Bigger moves | Heavy gifts, weapon strikes with bonus damage source |
| 4 | Heavy | Heavy Blow, signature attacks |
| 5+ | Exceptional — should have AP/energy cost matching | Reckless Charge (5 + self_damage 1), ultimate disciplines |

Wound tracks are 5-7 boxes; a 5-damage hit can KO a tough character
in one shot if it lands. Don't ladder damage faster than you ladder
costs or you create dominant strategies.

### Morale damage

Lower than HP damage typically — morale max is 20 but morale damage
sources are more plentiful. Standard range is 1-3, with 4+ for
signature mental attacks (Intimidate-style moves).

### AI weight

| Weight | Use for |
|---|---|
| 8 | DEF moves — defensive moves are picked situationally, not as defaults |
| 10 | CTL moves — control/utility |
| 12 | PWR moves — situational power plays |
| 15 | ATK moves — primary damage dealing |

Moves should follow the same convention so the AI behaves predictably.
Override only when the move is exceptionally strong or weak relative to
its category baseline (e.g., a 6-AP signature move might warrant AI_WEIGHT
20 to make sure the AI considers it).

### Tier magnitudes

Currently fixed at +10 / +20 / +30 (small/medium/large). Buffs at
combat-duration are stronger than round-duration because they persist
across multiple turns; round-duration buffs reward burst-turn
coordination but don't snowball.

### Self-damage

Pair with high HP damage — the trade is "bigger hit, you eat some
damage." Reckless Charge is the canonical pattern: 5 damage to target
+ 1 self damage at AP 6.

