## Validation checklist

Before testing in-game, verify:

- [ ] The hidden decision name matches the constructor's `DECISION` parameter exactly.
- [ ] The `SKILL_KEY` matches the suffix of the decision (e.g. decision `POD_combat_move_foo`, skill_key `foo`).
- [ ] All three loc keys exist (`<key>`, `<key>_desc`, `<key>_tooltip`).
- [ ] The `_desc` loc uses the macro: `[PODCombatMoveDesc('POD_combat_move_<key>')]`.
- [ ] The constructor block has all 7 parameters set.
- [ ] If the move deals HP damage, you set `hp_damage`. If it heals, you set `hp_heal` (with `TYPE`). If it buffs, you set a tier. If it stances, you set a flag. (A move with no setters compiles but does nothing when fired.)
- [ ] `team_enemy` / `team_ally` AoE moves use a damage value designed for *per-enemy* damage, not summed.
- [ ] If you set `retaliate_damage`, you also set the matching `retaliate_if_hit` or `retaliate_if_missed` flag.
- [ ] If the move is supernatural (auto-hit), the capability tags reflect that — `checks_stance` only, no `requires_hit_roll` and no `checks_guard`. Hit-chance comments don't matter because the move auto-hits.

In-game smoke test:

1. Load a fresh save with a character whose traits/perks satisfy your gate.
2. Open the Configure Combat Skills decision. The move should appear in the right column under your `CONFIG` section header.
3. Equip it. The card on the left side updates with your move.
4. Start a debug combat with the character. The move appears in the action bar.
5. Click the move. The expected effects fire — damage rolls, heal applies, buff stacks, etc.
6. Check the combat log for the resolution line.

If the move doesn't appear:

- Check the error log for unresolved decisions or loc keys.
- Verify the on_action wired your registration effect to game start.
- Confirm the gate isn't excluding your test character (try `always = yes` to isolate).

If the tooltip looks wrong:

- The `_desc` loc must call `PODCombatMoveDesc` — no other text.
- Reload the game (the macro reads the runtime story; if the move was registered late, the tooltip won't render until the catalogue is rebuilt).

